Spec: Private Android registration database sessions

Purpose:
  Back portable registry transactions with Android SQLite in private non-backup state.

Owns:
  ./RegistrationDatabase.java

Must:
  Keep state in a no-backup subdirectory with mode `0700` and reject linked registry paths.
  Open and close a session per operation, using immediate transactions and full synchronization without WAL.
  Commit only explicitly successful transactions and roll back failures on close.
  Bind SQL parameters, bound lookup rows and return fixed storage errors.
  Disable automatic corruption deletion/recreation and retain damaged state for explicit recovery.
